Z||000007||Cooter||08-07-2000||01:39 AM||||I cant believe they used the term "high value" in the same sentence as new F-bodies. Part of that article reminds me why I hate Car and Driver- the part about the full size GM sedans being hold overs from the 70's that almost brought the end of the big three. The end of those cars is the end of an era- If an import had those same features as the big dinosaurs, Car and Driver would be first to give them an award for it! Very few cars can compare to the ride quality from a frame with the body isolated from it as in the doomed Caprice and big Caddy. <P>Sorry about the ranting- but I found an 88 issue of C-and-D with the 88 Fiero Formula vs. the Mr.2- of course the Mr2 was the greatest thing since sliced bread and the revised Fiero was "another disappointment from GM. . . but that's what we expected"<P>------------------<BR>The slower they think you are, the more suprised they will be when you smoke them.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||08-07-2000||09:04 AM||||"Car and Driver" is turning into "SUV and Poser."  Nothing but trucks, SUVs, and German sedans I can't afford.  I had just about given up on them...then my last issue came, which had an Aston Martin, a Ferrari 360 F1 and a Porsche 911 Turbo on the cover.  I will probably have to endure 3 or 4 more months of trucks until I see more sports cars.<P>Nearly all automags waffled on the Fiero, but the worst of the lot was Car and Driver.  In a matter of two years they went from high praise to total damnation of the the Fiero.<P>I think Road and Track was kindest.  They pointed out the Fiero's flaws, but never, ever said the Fiero was a bad car.<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 08-07-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000009||HugGRRRFiero||08-07-2000||09:29 AM||||Car and Driver mentioned GM?...  I gota go read this!<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||HugGRRRFiero||08-07-2000||09:41 AM||||Figures...  I agree with ChadMan.  They're even putting Hype into the article about the new GM cars coming out soon.  In a few years they will tell us they suck too even if they DO turn out to be good cars.  Then they will tell us to go buy import cars that cost twice as much...  C&D, Insulting readers intelligence doesn't sell magazines, maybe it does? but I'm not buying.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||13
Z||000011||mrfixit58||08-07-2000||09:56 AM||||Unfortunatly, this isn't NEW news about GM. If you look at the big three and apply the qualities you would like to see in a first class automobile manufacturer, you'd have a hard time overlooking Chrysler. With the Viper, PT Cruser, Durango, Prowler, 300, and (and yes, the minivan :rolleyes <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> more, they are giving the people what they want.<P>Of course Ford is concentrating on buying up all the little companies most notabley Jaguar, and pushing the Ford Focus (yuk.. gag). The little Mustang is kicking but in the "afforable" performace car class and the Crown Vic (read - rear wheel drive) is still a hit with the Police and Geritol crowd.<P>Meanwhile, GM keeps producing copy-cat and cookie cutter cars with little to no style and charging the public more than the other two companies. <P>Just as a side note... did yo know that GM was producing a true 4-door S-10 pickup truck long before anyone else??. Yes, they were/are a big thing in South America. I read one article a few years ago where one guy wanted one so bad bought a new cab and the doors and had them shipped to the U.S. since they would not allow a complete truck into the country. He then lengthened a frame and built his own... complete with V-8 power. A couple of years later, the Dodge Durango comes out and is an instant success. Now, GM is once again trying to play catch-up.<P>If reliability were the only facter, I still think GM would win. Their motors, electronics, and transmissions are highly reliable. The cars are just too bland. And, for some reason, about the time something becomes interesting, GM kills it. I still can't beieve they are still aking the Camaro/Firebird. They can't sell them because they want more then the Mustang, but so far, they are still making them.<P>I'm Done,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
