Z||000013||pollock||08-07-2000||02:13 PM||||I hate the hell out of Car and Driver, Motor Trend, etc.  None of those magazines can get off the BMW/Acura teat.  <P>Shocked to see that they would print something even halfway positive about a Fiero.<P>I do have to agree that GM is incredibly sackless.<P>I see the wimpy, spongelike people who drive car&driver-type rides, and can't help but think that they wouldn't last 10 minutes driving my Mustang.  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||ChadMan||08-07-2000||03:00 PM||||And another thing.  Why is Car and Driver always kissing Audi's a$$?  They've got their noses so far up in there they're smelling yesterday's bratwurst and wienerschnitzel.  <P>Imagine C/D's reaction if GM took a lowly economy platform like the Cavalier/Sunfire chassis, gave it a homely body that's impossible to see out of and asked $35K for it.  Audi did just that in turning the Golf/New Beetle into the TT and C/D thinks it's the greatest thing since the Miata.||||reg||5
Z||000015||Pontiaddict||08-07-2000||03:37 PM|||| <B>"For the ZR-1, despite Chevrolet's quirky insistence that it remain externally indistinguishable (to all but the anointed) from more mundane brethren, was one of the most able high-performance road cars in history.</B> Thats why the Z06 is faster with  less horsepower, an all around better car, and WAAAAAAAAAAAAY cheaper. Everybody who thinks the LT5 was the greatest engine in the world needs to pull their heads out of their butts and realize that it was a giant, heavy, expensive turd! <P>What does Canadian race car drivers have to do with GM killing cars in their prime?<P>All this from a magazine that thinks <I>The Dodge Colt Vista of the 21st century</I> Pt Cruiser. Is another one of the greatest cars on the planet.<P>I don't really like C&D anyway. The only yuppie car mags that I want to read are Motor trend and Autoweek. Motor trend, not for the editotial, but for the fact that they usually  get the scoops on the newest happenings. Autoweek sucks, but it gives me something to do for 10 minutes a week.||||reg||8
Z||000016||87ECO5||08-07-2000||03:54 PM||||C'mon, <B>Pontiaddict</B>.  The LT-5 was an awesome powerplant.  Co-designed by Lotus and built by Mercury Marine, that beast pumped out over 400 high-RPM horsepower towards the end of ZR-1 production.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Of course, there was that little issue of maintenance.  I heard that, if a ZR-1 owner had problems with their engine, Chevy dealership mechanics weren't even allowed to touch them.  Instead, they were crated up and sent back to Mercury for repair or replacement!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000017||RobertVol||08-07-2000||11:13 PM||||Speaking of Car & Driver ...I think we should send them e mails over and over saying we want to see a retro article on the fiero and all the mods that can be done to them and how there are alot of people in love with them!STILL!<BR> Heck there over 1000 of us right here on the Forum! imagine filling up their mailbox with Fiero Lovers! I already sent them a comment about "so called" accurate article.<P>Can you imagine ? I think a retro article about Fieros and what they are now to their owners would be great !  ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Black88GT||08-07-2000||11:20 PM||||You guys have it all wrong.  Car and Driver praised the Fiero like no other in the April 1988 edition when it compared the Formula to the MR2 and the CRX.  After the 1984 bomb, no car mag. wanted anything to do with the Fiero.  Road and Track destroyed the Formula in their edition comparing it to the MR2 Supercharged.  Some excerts........<P>From Car and Driver....<P>Have we got a surprise for you.  The new Fiero Formula looks exactly like the flat-footed Pontiac two-seater that has been disappointing us for years-and it did finish last in this test.  But don't laugh up your sleeve (or write us a nasty letter) just yet: the same old body is home to a brand new soul.  The Fiero elicited oohs and ahs from all four editors.  "This thing is really improved," rejoiced Larry Griffin, and he speaks for all of us.<BR>    The Fiero acts like a different car now, because that's what it is.  The new suspension Pontiac has been promising us since its debut has finally arrived, and it transforms the Fiero Formula into an agile, confident road eater"<P>It goes into talking about the details of the suspension and says "The new Fiero feels as solid as Mount Rushmore" and "In fact, not much fazes this car anymore"<P>Now, Road and Track article.....<P>It goes onto a decent start talking about the suspension improvements and such.  Then its "The Fiero remains a wide, heavy car with slow steering not very subtle and not responsive to the light touch"  Then it says it can out handle the MR2 on light surfaces.  Makes no sense.  In the next 15 hundred paragraphs, it praised the MR2 SC like its a friggin Ferrari, with no mention of the door-stop like styling.  In the last couple paragraphs labeled "And the winner is...."  It says "Talk about David and Goliath.  In this battle the little Samurai hacks away at the giant without pity, swinging a sharp, swift sword.....in our ratings the Fiero didn't win a single driving category.  All 4 drivers preferred the MR2, evwn with price as a factor"<P>Those 4 drivers are idiots.  The price difference was $4,500!!!  You could drop a 3.8 SC in a Fiero for a little over that! Of course they didn't HAVE that engine then, but you get the point.  Almost forgot, the only victory for thr Fiero in the ratings categories was exterior styling, which the fiero got a 7.5 and the MR2 got a 7.2.  Yeah thats accurate.<P><BR>jeff                         <P>BTW I have had that "Alphabet soup..." article on my page for like 2 years.<BR>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               <BR>||||reg||1
